            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral pediatric Kienböck's disease: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>144-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/BPB.0b013e32835b5696</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bilateral Kienböck's disease in pediatrics is extremely rare. We report a case of a 14-year-old boy with bilateral pediatric Kienböck's disease who was treated by temporary scaphotrapeziotrapezoidal joint fixation, with a good clinical result and radiographic results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
